{
 "residual": [
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0001",
    "ADR-0002",
    "ADR-0003",
    "ADR-0004",
    "ADR-0009"
   ],
   "severity": "medium",
   "text": "The committed registry docs/registry/architecture.yaml is stale against the revised ADRs. This is expected until the TD-33 serial merge, but nothing is merged yet. (a) control_plane still reads `request_restore(payload, restore_epoch, expected_state_hash)`, while ADR-0002 line 203 has `expected_state_hash: int = 0, has_expected_hash: bool = false` and its log says 'registry signature revised'. (b) frame_order still reads 'INPUT_ADAPTER -100, TICK_DRIVER -50, PRESENTATION 0' with no HOST_SERVICE -40 (ADR-0001 line 80). (c) presentation_clock still reads 'tick_alpha, T, running' with no state or load_seq; the replacement exists only as a `revise_existing` block in ADR-0009 line 696. (d) block_registration lacks `register_key_space` and the BOOTING-only host registrar facet (ADR-0003 lines 328 and 331). (e) owner_callable_contract lists only `handlers(record, NotifyContext)`, not the subscriber form `(batch: ChangeBatch, ctx: NotifyContext) -> CompletionToken`. The frame_order and control_plane revisions are carried only as ADR-0006 candidates and ADR-0008 referenced_by notes. ADR-0001 and ADR-0002 are the owner ADRs of these entries and carry no Registry Candidates section of their own."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0005",
    "ADR-0010"
   ],
   "severity": "medium",
   "text": "The sorted-key helper has two incompatible definitions. ADR-0005 declares `CanonicalEncoder.sorted_int_keys` / `sorted_string_keys` (lines 156, 170, 420-421), which sit in canonical_encoder.gd. ADR-0010 \u00a7 5.3 (line 233) puts `sorted_int_keys` / `sorted_text_keys` in a separate `src/shared/det/sorted_keys.gd`, with its own allow-list entry for bare Array and `.keys()`. ADR-0010 OQ-N(2) still asks ADR-0005 to name them. The names (string vs text), the host file and the allow-list entry therefore disagree. ADR-0005 line 170 also says the regex bans the raw forms, so the lint has to know which file is the sanctioned site."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0005",
    "ADR-0010"
   ],
   "severity": "medium",
   "text": "ADR-0005 requires Variant pass-through signatures that ADR-0010 does not allow-list. ADR-0005 line 174 exempts 'canonical_encoder.gd ... and the named pass-through signatures'. Its Key Interfaces declare `Hash64.of_value(value: Variant)` in hash64.gd (line 427) and `canonical_encode(value: Variant)` on StateHasher / the kernel (line 459). ADR-0010 TD-13 puts only canonical_encoder.gd on dictionary_variant.json (SIM-09 row, line 292). The word 'pass-through' does not appear in ADR-0010. SIM-09 would flag hash64.gd and the kernel forwarder. ADR-0005 OQ-13 leaves the granularity to ADR-0010, and ADR-0010 OQ-H defers the contents."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0006",
    "ADR-0003"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "ADR-0003 TD-07(12) gives a host service a BOOTING-only `HostRegistrarFacet` limited to `register_fault_domain` (ADR-0003 lines 295 and 331). ADR-0006's `SaveService.setup(control, clock, wall_clock, block_versions, knobs)` (line 212) takes no registrar facet, so nothing wires fault domain 1. ADR-0006 line 422 still treats registering domain 1 from a module with no block as an unresolved assumption ('outside ADR-0003's stated examples')."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0008",
    "ADR-0009"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "The snap-flag space is stated differently. ADR-0008 line 132 says the flags snap in base-pixel space and 'Under pass A the viewport is the base-pixel field, so the same holds'. ADR-0009 Alternative 4 (line 430) says 'the snap flags snap in base-pixel space only under ADR-0008's pass B variant'. TD-20 required ADR-0009 to drop the unknown wording and cite ADR-0008; the 'only under pass B' restriction contradicts ADR-0008."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0009",
    "ADR-0004"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "ADR-0009 line 124 says the facet 'forwards to NotifyFacet.subscribe(cls, block_id, handler, name)'. ADR-0004 line 132 (and the ADR-0004 registry candidate) defines `NotifyFacet.subscribe(block_id, handler, name)`, with the class and perception_access fixed at issue by `Kernel.issue_notify_facet(cls, perception_access)`. The `cls` argument does not exist."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0010",
    "ADR-0009"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "PRES-03 (ADR-0010 line 314) bans `set_position(`, `set_global_position(`, `global_position =`, `translate(`, `global_translate(`, `move_local_x(`, `move_local_y(`, `set_offset(`, `offset =`, `position =` and `transform =`. ADR-0009 \u00a7 4 (line 305) says the lint 'must cover the whole engine API surface' and also names `set_transform()`, `set_global_transform()`, `set(\"position\")` and `Sprite2D.offset`. The first three are not tokens in PRES-03, and `global_transform =` is not listed either."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0010"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "ADR-0010 \u00a7 1.2 (line 137) opens 'These and only these kernel classes may be named from src/presentation/ ...' and lists `NotifyFacet` in that list. The same paragraph then says NotifyFacet is named only by src/game/ and PresentationFacet. The list should either omit it or mark it 'facets-internal'. The ARCH-08 row states the correct rule, and the edges.json data must follow the restricted reading."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0005",
    "ADR-0010"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "TD-12 says all pure determinism code lives in src/shared/det/. ADR-0005 (line 371-378) and ADR-0010 (lines 237, 239, 427, 734) both keep `IntMath` at `src/shared/int_math.gd`, outside det/. The two ADRs agree, so there is no conflict between them. It is a deviation from the ruling's literal wording, and DET-01's det/ path scope therefore does not cover IntMath."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0001",
    "ADR-0002",
    "ADR-0003",
    "ADR-0004",
    "ADR-0006",
    "ADR-0007",
    "ADR-0010"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "The Depends On / Enables tables are not symmetric. ADR-0004 Enables lists ADR-0006, but ADR-0006 lists ADR-0004 only as 'Related, not a dependency'. ADR-0001 Enables omits ADR-0007 and ADR-0010, which depend on it. ADR-0002 Enables omits ADR-0004, ADR-0009 and ADR-0010. ADR-0003 Enables omits ADR-0007 and ADR-0010. ADR-0005 Enables lists ADR-0007, but ADR-0007 does not yet depend on ADR-0005 (see unapplied). No cycle exists."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0001"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "ADR-0001 line 27 (Verification Required 1) still says the recorded `_process` order is 'adapter -> driver -> presentation'. The diagram (lines 119-138), Decision \u00a7 2 and the KRN-LAT-02 criterion (line 270) include SaveHost at HOST_SERVICE between the driver and presentation."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0008",
    "ADR-0009"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "Driver ownership is worded differently. ADR-0009 line 188 says PipelineRoot 'owns a PresentationDriver (RefCounted)'. ADR-0008 \u00a7 6.2 says 'The composition root constructs the PresentationDriver and injects it; PipelineRoot holds it'. The behaviour is compatible, but the construction site should be stated once."
  },
  {
   "adrs": [
    "ADR-0010",
    "ADR-0009",
    "ADR-0008"
   ],
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "PRES-01's exemption set (PipelineRoot, INPUT_SURFACE at INPUT_ADAPTER, layer-3/4 UI Controls) does not mention the debug layer 5. ADR-0008 \u00a7 6.3 says 'the debug layer (5) run[s] on engine process time'. ADR-0009 also has a DIAGNOSTIC class registered through PresenterDescriptor. A DIAGNOSTIC presenter with its own `_process` would fail PRES-01 as written. UNVERIFIED whether the intent is to exempt it; ADR-0009 owns the set."
  }
 ],
 "unapplied": [
  "TD-27 (ADR-0007 part): docs/architecture/adr-0007-static-content-data-pipeline-and-stable-type-ids.md is unmodified (git status). Its Depends On (line 33) is still 'ADR-0001, ADR-0003' with no 'ADR-0005 (golden content-hash vectors only; not an authoring dependency)'. Its Enables (line 34) does not list ADR-0006. ADR-0005 line 61 and ADR-0006 line 37 both assume these edits. ADR-0007 line 444 says in prose 'it depends on ADR-0005' but the table disagrees.",
  "TD-33 (registry merge): the Registry Candidates sections exist in ADR-0004, 0005, 0006, 0008, 0009 and 0010, but the committed docs/registry/architecture.yaml has none of the corrections yet. That is by design (the orchestrator merges serially), but ruling TD-05's 'Update the registry control_plane signature' and TD-04/TD-33's frame_order and presentation_clock values are not yet in the registry (see residual 1)."
 ],
 "notes": "I did not edit any file. All 34 rulings were checked by grep and bounded range reads against the owner ADR and each also_touch ADR. Every ruling except TD-27 (ADR-0007 part) is applied in its owner ADR and reflected in the also_touch ADRs. The ADRs also carry Review Log entries naming the TD ids, and I confirmed the body text separately.\\n\\nVerified applied, with the main anchors:\\n- TD-01: the explicit deny list is in ADR-0010 \u00a7 2.2 rule 4 and ARCH-08. The facets list matches ADR-0010 \u00a7 1.2. KeyBuf is at src/kernel/facets/key_buf.gd. ADR-0004 has the placement table, and ADR-0003 and ADR-0009 cite the facets paths.\\n- TD-02/TD-03/TD-20/TD-22/TD-23: PipelineRoot is the single host with one `_process` at ProcessPriority.PRESENTATION. CAMERA_SOLVE is stage 1. The frame_pre_draw handler only writes canvas_transform and the parallax offsets, and the fallback is stated. PRESENTATION_LATE appears only in negatives. OQ-D is withdrawn, and OQ-E, J and L are closed in ADR-0009. The probe wording, thread_model pin and 2^24 rule are in. post_restore is dropped.\\n- TD-04: the two-statement frame() wrapper and KRN-FRAME-END, PresentationClock.state and load_seq, HOST_SERVICE = -40, the KRN-05 known-node set with SaveHost, kernel_host.gd, and the SIM-02 pointer. All are applied.\\n- TD-05/TD-06/TD-07/TD-08/TD-09/TD-10/TD-11: in ADR-0002, ADR-0003, ADR-0004 and ADR-0006; the sentinel rule is in ADR-0005; the ADR-0010 side is applied.\\n- TD-12 through TD-19, TD-21, TD-24 through TD-26, TD-28 through TD-32 and TD-34: all applied.\\n\\nNot verified:\\n- The architecture.md Data Flow redraw and the GDD sync items (FT-20/AC-134, TR-pxl-015, PF D.14, HUD and Player Controller OQs). They are outside the ADR set.\\n- tr-baseline.md and tr-registry.yaml.\\n- Whether playtest builds run the SIM_WRITE_TRIPWIRE profile, and release-export, D3D12 and Steam Deck behaviour. The ADRs mark all of these UNVERIFIED and I did not probe them.\\n- I did not read the full text of every 100 KB+ ADR. I covered the rulings' anchor sections plus grep sweeps, so a stray stale sentence elsewhere in the large ADRs is possible.\\n- Residual findings that quote line numbers are against the working copy on 2026-10-28.\""
}
